{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/presentation.js';s=open(p).read().replace('txt(g, \"'`P${i + 1}`, x, bottom, c);'\"','txt(g, p.name ? String(p.name).slice(0, 12) : \"'`P${i + 1}`, x, bottom, c);'\"');open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# UFOh Orbit\n\nOpen the delivered HTML directly in a browser. It is self-contained and needs no server, downloads or account for solo or couch co-op.\n\nPilot an overconfident saucer through a complete four-sector mission. A complete blue ring protects one ram or missile. Shooting spends it; continuous fire keeps it empty. While recharging you move at half speed. The white cannon bead rotates clockwise toward your request. Break a cluster to make a chain. Gold command emitters are open targets.\n\n- Controller: left stick move, right stick aim, R2 or Cross fire, Options pause. PlayStation labels default; Xbox labels are in Controls.\n- Keyboard/mouse: WASD or arrows move, mouse aim, click or Space fire, Escape pause. All screens support mouse, keyboard and controller.\n- Touch: invisible left movement stick and right aim stick. Automatic aim and deliberate firing bursts preserve recharge opportunities. A rescue action appears beside an available wreck.\n- Local Co-op: choose keyboard+pad, two pads, or a split keyboard (P1 WASD/F; P2 arrows/period). A ready shield touching a wreck revives your partner. Both down ends the flight.\n- AI Hub: an embedded session launches automatically. Authority owns combat; guests send intent. Menus are local and shared time continues. World-changing dev tools are unavailable. Independent HTML does not supply a separate room service.\n\nMission and Score Attack have separate local records and six-character name entry. Storage denial leaves the game playable for the current visit. The title starts a 76-second real-simulation showcase after ten seconds idle; any intentional input returns to the menu.\n\nPause → Dev Mode provides tuning, invulnerability, actor/formation spawning, sector/wave/boss jumps, single stepping, playback speed, collision/aim overlays, input replay/snapshot export and validated content import/export. Dev and attract flights never enter score records. See \"'`docs/content.md` for content authoring, `docs/network.md` for authority and protocol details, and `docs/research.md` for historical evidence and unknowns.\n\nBuild from this folder with `npm run build`. The packaged root HTML and `build/game.html` are identical. `npm test` runs the complete suite, printing failures and one count line. Detailed reports and purposeful screenshots are under `artifacts/`. The installed Python Playwright environment is used without installing browsers. Read `docs/verification.md` for scope and limitations.\n\nThe native my-3D2dge engine is unmodified. Custom code uses its fixed-step timing, native scene/shell/input/settings/synth systems, pixel primitives, palette ramps, depth-sorted actors, material/shape registries, Path and tween/easing facilities. Full engine MIT notice and unchanged released Hub client are embedded in the HTML.\nEOF\ncat >> docs/dependencies.md <<'\"'EOF'\n\nBuild-only tooling: esbuild 0.25.12 (MIT), pinned in package-lock.json. It bundles game ESM modules; the released Hub client is inserted verbatim afterward and receives no transformation. Runtime uses no CDN assets or third-party raster/audio resources. Native browser Canvas2D and Web Audio provide presentation and synthesis.\nEOF\ncat > docs/verification.md <<'EOF'\n# Verification evidence\n\n\"'`npm test` is the single quiet coordinator. It runs deterministic simulation tests, adapter tests, foundation/storage/native headless draw tests, offline native-audio checks, browser input/UI checks and the official AI Hub harness with custom shared gameplay checks. `artifacts/test-report.json` retains the consolidated count and individual evidence.\n\nThe solo full-mission proof uses actual movement/aim/fire inputs from a deterministic pilot, canonical hull and shield balance, no invulnerability or dev commands. Milestones require shots, a shield ram, fusion, propagated chains, gunship destruction, all three boss phases, extraction and victory. An exported full input replay reconstructs its exact final simulation snapshot. A separate two-player proof performs a real rescue, then finishes with one survivor. Additional seeds, defeat/retry, extended score attack, content validation and actor cleanup have scenario checks.\n\nThe native engine headless renderer draws every enemy, shields, boss components and cosmetic effects on its stand-in context, asserts no drawing errors, and checks that repeated drawing never changes a simulation snapshot. Browser screenshots answer visual questions only: 1920×1080 title, first-contact readability and crowded command encounter.\n\nUI tests use a standard-mapped synthetic pad, desktop keyboard and mouse, phone/tablet touch emulation and Firefox/WebKit smoke checks. Touch contacts retain independent left/right owners. These are stand-ins; no physical controller, TV, phone, tablet or iPhone was available.\n\nAudio tests render the actual original native synth definitions in OfflineAudioContext and check nonzero, finite, bounded output, different cues, bus gain, 10% first-run music, mute and cleanup. No human listening evaluation occurred. Historical source sound remains unknown.\n\nHub tests run the original pinned conformance harness against the generated HTML, on an owned 127.0.0.1 server with an OS-selected port. Cases cover one/two players, latency150/jitter50/loss5, host departure and a dedicated server host with no pilot. Custom two-page play checks authority dimensions during resize, remote aim and movement, shared score/cascades, rescue, fusion, boss phases, extraction/results, no simulation freeze beneath a local overlay, and post-end traffic/audio cleanup. Network evidence is local transport emulation, not a real internet session.\n\nNo frame-rate target or performance benchmark is part of acceptance. Detailed traces, screenshots and protocol snapshots remain within this development folder.\nEOF\nbiome format --write src/presentation.js > artifacts/biome-final.log\nnode tools/build.mjs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
