{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > .npmrc <<'EOF'\nloglevel=silent\nEOF\ncat > UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456/.npmrc <<'EOF'\nloglevel=silent\nEOF\ncat > UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456/docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Fixed issue ledger\n\nSeven distinct defects were found by automated or visual testing:\n\n1. Native \"'`start({boot:false})` left the upstream engine'\"'s booting flag active, so requested scenes never entered. **Critical.** Start with ordinary native scenes and omit that option; engine stays unmodified. Actual file:// start/play and Hub traffic prove the correction.\n2. An arena background queued as an overlay obscured actors. Use native floor decals so actors remain bright above it. Visual screenshot review.\n3. Content validation rejected an authored pincer's spacing. Align the documented range with legitimate formations. Canonical deck validation.\n4. Projectile cleanup preceded swept collision, dropping a very fast crossing hit. Resolve swept collisions first. High-speed segment scenario.\n5. Drifters recomputed their original velocity and stuck to rails. Retain reflected velocity. Boundary scenario and full missions.\n6. Dev spawning discarded explicit speed. Carry it into the spawned actor. Spawn scenario.\n7. Quick fire press/release between fixed updates was lost by held-only input polling. Accept native pressed OR down. Split-keyboard quick-tap browser regression.\n\nNine more corrections came from integration review and received regression coverage:\n\n- Set native \"'`game.live` as well as its options field for Hub overlays. **Critical:** a local pause could otherwise freeze authority.\n- Normalize remote aim vectors while retaining bearing, rather than clamping their axes independently.\n- Map a guest'\"'s first local device to its assigned world pilot, including mouse and touch aiming.\n- Guard audio scene/unlock calls after Hub end so ended audio cannot restart.\n- Attempt audio unlock from meaningful gamepad input, with idempotent gesture handling.\n- Clamp existing boss component health on balance reset, using the same policy as a live slider change.\n- Stop showing rescue cues for a departed, inactive pilot.\n- Keep the predicted shield exposed while held fire awaits acknowledgement.\n- Measure Unicode snapshot fragments in encoded bytes when enforcing protocol limits.\n\nTwo critical defects in total were corrected. A source setup-script typo and corrected test-selector, canonical mode-name, and viewport-shape assumptions are not counted as game defects.\nEOF\ncat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Verification in progress (final integration)\n- Simulation61scenarios pass, including exact full-mission input replay, additional seeds, genuine2p rescue and one-survivor victory.\n- Hub18unit checks; original harness80checks; custom two-page19checks includes real co-op combat, loss/jitter, resize/aim, local pause, boss/extraction, active-audio end cleanup.\n- Audio35offline/native checks. UI controller20/20,keyboard/dev37/37,records10/10,local co-op9/9 targeted after fixes; full UI coordinator running.\n- \"'`npm test` consolidated run active (owned exec session94703). All detailed evidence written under dev/artifacts.\n- Fixed issue ledger: docs/issues.md. Seven defects caught by tests/visual checks; nine additional integration-review fixes; two critical total. Native engine untouched.\n- Final tasks: inspect consolidated result; fill interview and in-game feedback consistently; build exact root artifact; final package/About/standalone smoke; update progress complete.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > .npmrc <<'EOF'\nloglevel=silent\nEOF\ncat > UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456/.npmrc <<'EOF'\nloglevel=silent\nEOF\ncat > UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456/docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n# Fixed issue ledger\n\nSeven distinct defects were found by automated or visual testing:\n\n1. Native \"'`start({boot:false})` left the upstream engine'\"'s booting flag active, so requested scenes never entered. **Critical.** Start with ordinary native scenes and omit that option; engine stays unmodified. Actual file:// start/play and Hub traffic prove the correction.\n2. An arena background queued as an overlay obscured actors. Use native floor decals so actors remain bright above it. Visual screenshot review.\n3. Content validation rejected an authored pincer's spacing. Align the documented range with legitimate formations. Canonical deck validation.\n4. Projectile cleanup preceded swept collision, dropping a very fast crossing hit. Resolve swept collisions first. High-speed segment scenario.\n5. Drifters recomputed their original velocity and stuck to rails. Retain reflected velocity. Boundary scenario and full missions.\n6. Dev spawning discarded explicit speed. Carry it into the spawned actor. Spawn scenario.\n7. Quick fire press/release between fixed updates was lost by held-only input polling. Accept native pressed OR down. Split-keyboard quick-tap browser regression.\n\nNine more corrections came from integration review and received regression coverage:\n\n- Set native \"'`game.live` as well as its options field for Hub overlays. **Critical:** a local pause could otherwise freeze authority.\n- Normalize remote aim vectors while retaining bearing, rather than clamping their axes independently.\n- Map a guest'\"'s first local device to its assigned world pilot, including mouse and touch aiming.\n- Guard audio scene/unlock calls after Hub end so ended audio cannot restart.\n- Attempt audio unlock from meaningful gamepad input, with idempotent gesture handling.\n- Clamp existing boss component health on balance reset, using the same policy as a live slider change.\n- Stop showing rescue cues for a departed, inactive pilot.\n- Keep the predicted shield exposed while held fire awaits acknowledgement.\n- Measure Unicode snapshot fragments in encoded bytes when enforcing protocol limits.\n\nTwo critical defects in total were corrected. A source setup-script typo and corrected test-selector, canonical mode-name, and viewport-shape assumptions are not counted as game defects.\nEOF\ncat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Verification in progress (final integration)\n- Simulation61scenarios pass, including exact full-mission input replay, additional seeds, genuine2p rescue and one-survivor victory.\n- Hub18unit checks; original harness80checks; custom two-page19checks includes real co-op combat, loss/jitter, resize/aim, local pause, boss/extraction, active-audio end cleanup.\n- Audio35offline/native checks. UI controller20/20,keyboard/dev37/37,records10/10,local co-op9/9 targeted after fixes; full UI coordinator running.\n- \"'`npm test` consolidated run active (owned exec session94703). All detailed evidence written under dev/artifacts.\n- Fixed issue ledger: docs/issues.md. Seven defects caught by tests/visual checks; nine additional integration-review fixes; two critical total. Native engine untouched.\n- Final tasks: inspect consolidated result; fill interview and in-game feedback consistently; build exact root artifact; final package/About/standalone smoke; update progress complete.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('src/data/interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['tech']='JavaScript/Canvas2D/Web Audio; my-3D2dge v0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691), AI Hub session client v1.4.0 (35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869); esbuild 0.25.12 build-only'\nd['sourceInformation']['animation']='Native 120 Hz engine clock, tween/easing, Path, and procedural banking, orbital lights, shield/fusion/chain/boss motion'\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='1–2-player AI Hub shared-world authoritative co-op with prediction/interpolation; standalone simultaneous couch co-op'\nd['sourceInformation']['research']='Original UFO\"'! manual and archival record/reviews, gameplay and regional box images inspected; audiovisual recording access failed, so exact historical audio is unknown. Evidence matrix in docs/research.md.'\"'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unrestricted headless checks: deterministic legal-input complete missions/replay, co-op rescue/survivor victory, emulated pad/touch, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit, offline native audio, official Hub harness and two-page lossy gameplay. No physical devices, real internet session or human listener.'\nd['testingFeedback']=['Seven defects were caught by automated or visual testing and fixed; nine additional integration-review corrections are recorded in docs/issues.md.','Two critical defects were fixed overall: native boot-option scene blocking (found by testing), and paused shared-world authority (found by review).','The canonical full-mission legal-input playthrough and exact replay proved all combat interactions, every boss phase, extraction and victory without debug shortcuts.','Static string-presence packaging checks gave less behavioral evidence than input-driven journeys; they remain useful for metadata and client placement.']\nd['engineFeedback']=['Native pixel primitives, hue-shifted palette ramps, depth-sorted art and a complete controller/settings/synth foundation.','Yes. The documented boot:false route retained the engine booting flag and intercepted scene changes; ordinary scene startup fixed it. An initial overlay also obscured actors until moved to native decals.','The authoritative shield, collision, chain, encounter and simultaneous co-op simulation, plus replay and Hub state replication.','Keeping a fixed authoritative arena and clear native art across changing device shapes while separating presentation from multiplayer authority.','none; the vendored engine and released Hub client are unmodified. Game-specific systems extend their public APIs.','Provide a simultaneous shared-world arcade starter with authority-aware pause and an explicit validated viewport transform.']\nd['promptFeedback']=['Concrete mechanical pillars, source boundaries and end-to-end verification requirements made the intended game clear.','The engine starter uses viewport-derived arena bounds and alternating arcade players; the authored game requires fixed bounds and simultaneous pilots, so those defaults needed explicit replacement.','Integrating deterministic shield and chain combat with controller/touch menus and correct remote authority across the entire mission.','Prioritize the acceptance checks and put the final delivery naming and shared simulation contract together in one concise handoff.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n');pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Interview schema filled: 15 source fields, 4 testing, 6 engine, 4 prompt answers.')\nPY\nrg -n 'TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub|Verification in progress|final findings' src docs README.md --glob '\"'!interview.json'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
