tive pixel primitives, hue-shifted palette ramps, depth-sorted art and a complete controller/settings/synth foundation.','Yes. The documented boot:false route retained the engine booting flag and intercepted scene changes; ordinary scene startup fixed it. An initial overlay also obscured actors until moved to native decals.','The authoritative shield, collision, chain, encounter and simultaneous co-op simulation, plus replay and Hub state replication.','Keeping a fixed authoritative arena and clear native art across changing device shapes while separating presentation from multiplayer authority.','none; the vendored engine and released Hub client are unmodified. Game-specific systems extend their public APIs.','Provide a simultaneous shared-world arcade starter with authority-aware pause and an explicit validated viewport transform.']\nd['promptFeedback']=['Concrete mechanical pillars, source boundaries and end-to-end verification requirements made the intended game clear.','The engine starter uses viewport-derived arena bounds and alternating arcade players; the authored game requires fixed bounds and simultaneous pilots, so those defaults needed explicit replacement.','Integrating deterministic shield and chain combat with controller/touch menus and correct remote authority across the entire mission.','Prioritize the acceptance checks and put the final delivery naming and shared simulation contract together in one concise handoff.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n');pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Interview schema filled: 15 source fields, 4 testing, 6 engine, 4 prompt answers.')\nPY\nrg -n 'TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub|Verification in progress|final findings' src docs README.md --glob '\"'!interview.json'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"Interview schema filled: 15 source fields, 4 testing, 6 engine, 4 prompt answers.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
