{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# UFOh Orbit — final verification\n\n## Delivery identity\n- Chosen with real random selection from 50 silent title candidates: **UFOh Orbit**.\n- Dev folder: \"'`UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456/`.\n- Root final HTML: `UFOh-Orbit-UFO-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-034456.html`.\n- Root interview: `exit-interview.json`; identical to dev `src/data/interview.json`.\n- All source, tests, docs, dependencies, caches and evidence are inside dev folder. Root retains only prescribed inputs/progress/deliverables.\n\n## Current action / resume here\n- **Exact final candidate is built and source is frozen.** Latest `npm test` is running in owned exec session **82074**; poll it with write_stdin. Expected around 420 checks; use the actual result, not this estimate.\n- Once it passes: inspect `artifacts/test-report.json`, confirm no failures, update this file with final count, and deliver root HTML + interview in final chat. Include required Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in chat (all full answers are also in interview and in-game credits).\n- Do not rebuild or change source unless a genuine failure requires it. Any source change needs affected checks after rebuilding.\n\n## Complete systems\n- Native my-3D2dge v0.89.1 scene/shell/controller/settings/render/synth foundation, unmodified engine revision `8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691` and MIT notice retained.\n- Exact unmodified AI Hub v1.4.0 client revision `35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869`, first script immediately after charset. Protocol metadata1–2/shared-world.\n- Fixed authoritative960×540arena, steering/clockwise delayed cannon, real-bead shots, shield/recharge speed tradeoff, hull/grace/immunity, swept contacts, unique chains and scores, fusion/hunters/gunships, three-phase command craft.\n- Four authored sectors, complete victory/extraction, defeat/retry, score-attack deck and independent records, six-character typing/controller wheel, storage denial handling.\n- Simultaneous local co-op with explicit device pairing, real rescue, team score/contribution; Hub host authority/guest prediction and interpolation, dedicated no-pilot server, fixed bounds across resize, leave/time-up/end cleanup.\n- Native procedural shaded saucers/threats/boss/beacons, star/planet field, native Path/tween/easing, launch/recoil/ring/fusion/chain/warning animations, code-generated music/SFX/gibberish with matching HUD subtitles. Music defaults10%.\n- Controller-first title/pause/settings/rebindings/results/credits, PlayStation/Xbox labels, keyboard/mouse, invisible twin touch sticks with safe-burst assistance and contextual rescue. Touch pause clears contacts. Guest quick taps survive between10Hzpackets.\n- Pause Dev Mode:16balance knobs, resets/clamps, invulnerability/refill/spawns/clear, sector/wave/boss jumps, timeline preview/step/speed, seed/encounter reset, collision/aim overlays, snapshot/input-replay export, validated JSON content import/export. Hub read-only diagnostics.\n- Ten-second title idle starts76-second real-simulation attract loop; all input categories cancel/consume it. Canonical defaults, no record contamination.\n- Full in-game Source Information +4Testing/6Engine/4Prompt answers; source details are paginated for controller readability. Same interview schema filled and validated.\n\n## Evidence and tests\n- Single command from dev: `npm test`. Quiet coordinator prints failures plus one count line; verbose evidence stays in dev/artifacts.\n-61simulation checks: canonical legal solo mission victory415.4s/score1086;202shots,1ram,2fusions,109chainkills,13gunships,all3boss phases; exact entire mission replay reconstructs final snapshot. Additional seeds and genuine co-op rescue followed by one-survivor victory. No dev shortcuts in whole-mission proofs.\n-22Hub unit checks after guest-fire-latch